You can create a function in JavaScript that returns all the factors of a given number by iterating through all numbers from 1 to the given number and checking if they divide the given number without leaving a remainder. This will give you all the factors. Here's how you can do it:

```javascript
function factors(n) {
    let factors = [];
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i === 0) {
            factors.push(i);
        }
    }
    return factors;
}

// Example usage:
console.log(factors(10)); // Output: [1, 2, 5, 10]
```

This function will return an array of all factors of the given number.
